      "created_at": "2026-04-08T20:55:38.597696Z",
      "resolved_at": "2026-04-08T21:02:03.469207Z",
      "resolution": "{\"action\": \"approve\", \"context\": \"## Resolved Questions\\n\\n**Decision 1: ContainerBackend interface type**\\nAnswer: Python Protocol (structural typing) — easier mocking, more Pythonic, no inheritance required. Reviewer_agent_design also recommends this.\\n\\n**Decision 2: Shared filesystem for worktrees**\\nAnswer: PVCs with k3s local-path provisioner (already decided). For single-node k3s this uses local-path StorageClass. RWX can be added for GKE later.\\n\\n**Decision 3: Dockerfiles and image build strategy**\\nAnswer: Keep Dockerfiles unchanged (Option A). They produce OCI images regardless of runtime. Add make targets that do docker build + k3s ctr images import.\\n\\n**Decision 4: GHCR image publishing**\\nAnswer: Leave release-images.yml as-is (Option A). GHCR is Docker-registry-compatible regardless of runtime.\\n\\n**Decision 5: .git shadow mount in k8s**\\nAnswer: Init container creates the shadow mount (Option A). Agent pod init container sets up tmpfs overlay before main container starts. Cleanest k8s-native approach.\\n\\n**Decision 6: Integration test infrastructure**\\nAnswer: k3s in CI with dedicated test namespace (Option A). Same runtime as local dev. No kind, no docker-compose for tests.\\n\\n**Feedback 1: Scope and timeline**\\nAnswer: Timeline is flexible, multi-week is fine. No upcoming features depend on Docker stability. sandbox/egg_lib/runtime.py CLI code should be migrated in this PR — full Docker removal means no Docker dependencies remain.\\n\\n**Feedback 2: Developer experience**\\nAnswer: k3s only (confirmed). macOS/Windows users use Lima/Rancher Desktop/WSL2. make k3s-setup handles Calico CNI installation automatically.\\n\\n**Feedback 3: Gateway session binding**\\nAnswer: Token-only auth is part of this migration (confirmed). IP-based binding removed. No additional security review needed — tokens are already the primary auth mechanism, IP binding was defense-in-depth.\"}",
      "phase": "refine",
      "content_changed": null
    },
